nt to Colombia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/41642"} "Helmut Bellingrodt"] ", the first Olympic medal won by a Colombian athlete. Bellingrodt would win the World Championship in 1974, and in 1978 he and his two brothers, Horst and " [:a {:href "/athletes/41641"} "Hanspeter (Bellingrodt)"] ", won the team event for Colombia at the Worlds."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Slow Run Points"] [:th {} "Slow Run Course 1 Points"] [:th {} "Slow Run Course 2 Points"] [:th {} "Slow Run Course 3 Points"] [:th {} "Fast Run Points"] [:th {} "Fast Run Course 1 Points"] [:th {} "Fast Run Course 2 Points"] [:th {} "Fast Run Course 3 Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "401"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/44548"} "Yakov Zheleznyak"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "569"] [:td {} "289"] [:td {} "96"] [:td {} "97"] [:td {} "96"] [:td {} "280"] [:td {} "93"] [:td {} "93"] [:td {} "94"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "58"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/41642"} "Helmut Bellingrodt"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/COL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/COL.png"}] "COL"]] [:td {} "565"] [:td {} "286"] [:td {} "97"] [:td {} "94"] [:td {} "95"] [:td {} "279"] [:td {} "93"] [:td {} "92"] [:td {} "94"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "135"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42350"} "John Kynoch"]] [:td {} [:a {